What’s your approach to A/B testing in email marketing? work on the fundamentals first (subject lines for open rate, CTA for CTR, etc. 

I always start by focusing on the fundamentals. That means testing elements that directly impact performance at each stage of the funnel:

* Subject lines to optimize open rates
* Preview text to support the hook
* CTAs and button placement to improve click-through rates
* Hero images or headline copy to test visual and messaging impact
* Send times to match audience behavior

Once those basics are dialed in, I move on to deeper tests like content length, offer positioning, and segmentation strategies. I typically let tests run until statistical significance is reached, and always track results in context—not just open or click rates, but also how each version affects revenue, conversions, and downstream metrics.



